      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-06-21_WidnesExaminer_art0138" n="art0138">
        <head>SUMMER MONTHS.</head>
        <p>SUMMER MONTHS.</p>
        <p>If you find that your system is unable to bear the oppressive heat, and you are almost unable to follow your vocation, immediately strengthen your constitu- tion by taking a, course of Gwilym E91119' Quinine Bitters. This preparation makes the weak strong, and gives new !scut and "go " to the weary toiler. It revives the spirits and strengthens the nerves, and by giving tone to the whole constitution, wards off fevers, and many other ailments prevalent at this time of the year. No family should to without a bottle in the 'bonne. An occasional dose, taken when feeling slightly out of sorts, has prevented many a long illness. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is The Best Remedy of The Age for Weakness, Nervousness, Indigestion, LOW Spirits, • Sleeplessness, Influenza, and Chest Affections. It is aften asked, " How is it that, one single medicine like •Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is capable of curing so many different diseases ?" The reply,however,is simple 'enough. Most diseases have a common source, either in a deranged stomach and its connections, or in weak and impure blood. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, by striking at the root of the evil, by strengthening the stomach and punfyinp the blood, places these impor- tant life sources in proper working order, and the disease, under whatever form it may have shown itself, disappears: Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is sold by all chemists and stores, in bottles 2s. 9d. and 4s.6d.each. Refuse to takesubstitutes. OUR FOOD.</p>
        <p>Constant overworking of the stomach must produce disease of that organ. More nutriment is furnished to the body by a small quantity of food well digested than be a large quantity half digested. The only trustsvoi thy and permanent remedy is Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, which, acting upon the digestive organs, strengthens them and stimulates them to health) action and gives tone to the whole stomach, impartinz new life, hope, strergth, and happiness. Overwork ought to be overpaid. Nature insists upon payment of her dues. Intense devotion to business gives the digestive organs , only a bare chance to perform their work. He who comes in a hurry from active work, rapidly swallows his food and hurries cut again, is piling up a debt which Nature makes him pay in a painful dyspepticesperience, Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters will help you to pay, and sooner you take it the better. Delicate patients often complain that they are unable to take quinine, as it produces headaches, kc., but it iris been established beyond doubt that Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters has overcome this difficulty, containing, as it does other medicinal herbs of great therapeutic value,such as sarsa- parilla, saffron, dandelion, gentian. and lavender, scien- tifically prepared in happy proportiors. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is sold in bottles 23. 9J. and ‘ls. '6i each, by all chemists and stores. Beware of imitations. The name " Gwilym Evans" must be found on the label, swam, and battle, to insure its being genuine., When you find the name, then you are sure there i 3, no mistake. The Sole Proprietors are The Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Company, Limited, Llanelly, South Wales.</p>
