      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-06-21_WidnesExaminer_art0180" n="art0180">
        <p>latters to the Suter.</p>
        <p>NOTICE TO CORRESPONDENTS.</p>
        <p>Authors of letters intended for publication must in all cases send their names and addresses to the Editor. Matters intonded for publication must be written 071 one aide only of the paper and sent in, if possible not later than Thursday. Correspondents are strongly advised to write briefly. A short letter has much greater chance of insertion than a long one. We cannot under ordinary circumstances under- take to return the manuscripts which are not used.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-06-21_WidnesExaminer_art0181" n="art0181">
        <head>Corporation Contracts.</head>
        <p>Corporation Contracts.</p>
        <p>Sir,—Much complaint has been made that those who are not satisfied with the proceedings of the Corporation during the last few years have not namPd individuals of whose conduct they did not approve. Is there a desire to induce some one who only wishes to promote the public weal to make a mistake or say something that might possibis be turned into a libel? Is there not a de- sire to prevent the fair and free discussion of public matters ? It is not for personal quarrels but for the public welfare that we care, and it is with the collective action of the Corporation, that the ratepayers have to deal. A great deal has been said about legality and illegality as if legality was the standard of right as gold is the standard of commercial value. It is legal for a man to stay ont every night until twelve o'clock and to spend more than half his income on himself, to be a tyrant in his house, and to do a great many abominable things. It is legal far a man to sell to a friend his shares in a company that he knows is going down for many times their value. It is legal for a man to com- mit sins so heinous that we do not care to mention them, and to be guilty of conduct so dishonourable and vile as to cause him to hold a place in the estimation of honourable men " for which a fiend might not in repu- tation change." To assume or argue that it is right in public life to do what is legal is an insult to the moral sense of the ratepayers. It is so very low, it is like obscenity, it is di4gusting and I for one will not be de- graded by giving it a moment's countenance. lam sorry such an argument should have been used in refer- ence to the Corporation of a town in which I have lived for more than thirty years.—Yours S. KENYON.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-06-21_WidnesExaminer_art0182" n="art0182">
        <head>MR. AND MRS. BALDWIN</head>
        <p>MR. AND MRS. BALDWIN</p>
        <p>OF WALSALL.</p>
        <p>THE LATTER A MEDICAL NURSE FOR MANY YEARS, WERE BOTH CURED IN A RATHER REMARKABLE MANNER BY VENO'S SEAWEED TONIC AND VENO'S LIGHTNING COUGH CURE. THEY TAKE GREAT PLEASURE IN RECOMMEND- ING VENO'S REMEDIES, AND BEING WELL KNOWN, AND HIGHLY RESPECTED CITIZENS, THEIR TESTIMONY IS THE MORE VALUABLE. Mr. J Baldwin, 9, Hall-lane. Walsall, writes. March 29th. The Veno Drug Co., Dear Sirs :—I have been suffering a long time with headaches, and biliousness. and have tried several remedies without any effect. I saw your advertisement in the Walsall paper and got a bottle of Veno's Seaweed Tonic, the effect upon me was marvellous. My head was better in a few hours, and my general health is much improved. Mrs Baldwin also wishes to add her testimony with regard to the great benefit she has received both from Veno's Seaweed Tonic and Veno's Lightning Cough Cure. She has been a Medical and Surgical Nurse for many years. She is able to speak with confidence about remedies, and she will have great pleasure in recommending them to all her friends. VENO'S SEAWEED TONIC .</p>
        <p>cures all ailments arising from a diseased condition of the stomach, liver, kidneys. and blood, such as indi— gestion, wind, costiveness, sluggish liver, headache, de- pression of spirits, impure blood, weak and painful back, palpitation, fullness after eating,nervousness, and general weakness. It has a wonderful tonic and strengthening effect. Price is lid and 2s 9d,ver bottle. VENO'S LIGHTNING COUGH CURE will stop an ordinary cough in one night, and cure chronic coughs, bronchitis, asthma, influenza, and whooping cough rapidly. Its vast superiority over the ordinary cough mixtures and the different emulsions cannot be estimated. It has saved thousands of lives after they have been turned out of hospitals. It is a new scientific remedy endorsed and recommended by do3tors. Price is lid and 2s 9d per bottle. A valuable book accompanies each bottle on the 'cure of diseases. Sold by Boots, Lmited, Warrington ; Peake, Earlestown and Newton ; Weston and Co. .Runcorn; Wallbridge,chemist, J W Jackson, chemist an 3 druggist, St Helens, and all chemists.</p>
