        <p>Warrington Junior Conservative Association. —Annual Excursion. An enjoyable time was spent by the members and friends of the Warrington Junior Conservative Association on Saturday on the occasion of the annual excursion to Southport. About 120 left the Central Station at halt-past one, and on arrival at Southport separated in search of the varied pleas- ures which the fashionable watering place affords. The weather was ideal,and nothing was wanting to make the visit thoroughly successful. At five o'clock the party gathered together at the Scarisbrick Hotel for tea. The manager of this well-known establishment provided an excellent meal, and the keen appetites of the visitors proved quite equal to the occasion. In th 3 unavoidable alhence of the President (Mr Roger C Parr), Councillor John Roberts presided, and there were also present— Alderman Sutton, Councillor Smethurst, Mr James Roberts, Mr and Mrs Holbrook, Mr Hamblett, and Messrs Williams, Thorley, Strettle, Hampson, Bate, Rogerson, Houghton, Brooks. and H Hayes (secre- tary). These last-named gentlemen formed the committee, and the admirable arrangements they made were responsible for much of the success of the excursion.—After tea several addresses were delivered. The party arrived home about ten o' clock .</p>
